this.add({id:1102, 
title:"HTTP Header Profile", 
body:" http header profile http headers used in  real-time protection policies to match various fields http request response headers. currently, configuring real-time protection policy, list available attributes based traits source web-client (user, os, browser) destination web-domain (app, activity, category). you create combinations policy attributes enforce security compliance objectives. the http header profile expands framework with option specify evaluate headers real-time processing web traffic. this provides granular control making available include parameters existing parameters. once http header profile created, select real-time protection policy. creating http header profiles to create http header profile, navigate policies > http header . click button. the new http header profile page opens. enter name http header profile. use tabs specify http header fields want match against. all header \"and\"ed together, values single field \"or\"ed together. no wildcard substring support time, exact match only. the following table lists describes examples fields available request response tabs creating new http header profile. field attribute type value example accept-encoding string arbiter (exact match) case-insensitive gzip deflate host string arbiter (exact match) case-insensitive en.wikipedia.org:8080 en.wikipedia.org referer string arbiter (exact match) case-insensitive http:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/main_page method string arbiter (exact match) case-insensitive post content-encoding string arbiter (exact match) case-insensitive gzip content-type string arbiter (exact match) case-insensitive application\/x-www-form-urlencoded origin string https:\/\/www.google.com upgrade string arbiter (exact match) case-insensitive example 1 upgrade: websocket example 2 upgrade: http\/2.0, shttp\/1.3, irc\/6.9, rta\/x11 in request tab, default request fields method host . click add request fields dropdown add fields. in response tab, default response field content-type . click add response fields dropdown add fields. for certain header fields, click + add add attributes field. you create custom http header fields profile, allows additional standard fields. once extended http headers feature enabled create new fields, can't downgraded. all existing header profiles created prior upgrading migrated continue work. to add custom header field: click custom add request fields add response fields dropdown. the new custom header field appears. enter new header field. the unique different existing default fields. select attribute dropdown enter value custom field. you configure following attributes field: regex : enter regular expressions want match against. exact match : enter values want match against, separated commas. numerical : select operator enter numerical values want match against. click + add add attributes field. you configure regex exact match attributes field. however, can’t add numerical attributes with regex exact match attributes. you use http header profiles block webdav traffic. netskope recommends blocking methods headers policy. to block webdav traffic: on new http header profile page, request tab. in method field, select methods defined webdav extension. available http include: move, copy, mkcol, propfind, proppatch, lock, unlock. (optional) you select additional header fields block webdav traffic. click add request fields add response fields select configure webdav headers. keep mind header fields \"and\"ed together, values single field \"or\"ed together. available headers include: dav, depth, destination, if, lock-token, overwrite. click save add http header profile profiles list. using http header page from http header list page: (optional) you sort http header profiles profile names. click ellipses end profile edit delete http header profile. you select checkbox left profile names bulk delete profiles. adding http header profiles real-time protection policies you add any http header profile real-time protection policy. navigate real-time protection policies list page. http header profiles encapsulate different fields header. click http header field add list. if any existing profiles, create directly policy creation page. click gear icon open http header profiles list page separate tab. see real-time protection topic additional information creating policies. " });
