this.add({id:1182, 
title:"The Kill Chain & How the Cloud Affects It", 
body:" the kill chain & how cloud affects it the typical kill chain involves stages: recon : typically used targeted attacks, attackers gather intelligence victims. this stage involve social engineering (e.g., learning weaknesses victims exploited deliver malicious payloads). the growing adoption cloud services gives additional entry points. in phase, actors research look publicly accessible resources. weaponize : the malicious actors prepare attack vectors (e.g., develop payload). this phase involves preparation infrastructure. in original model, tasks involve registration domains staging exploit kits. today, cloud services increasingly used distribute malware host c2 infrastructures (see delivery phase), so play important role well. delivery : the malicious payload delivered designated victim. before cloud advent, phase involves drive-by (targeted), watering-hole (opportunistic) attacks, spear phishing campaigns. today pages served services (see netskope blog ), similarly cloud services used host malicious payloads. another way exploit phase create fake application login pages (mimicking ones victims) with purpose lure victim phish credentials. exploit : the attack vector exploited. if involves malicious executable bait document, artifact clicked victim, executed, action performed. exploit kit, vulnerability endpoint (or browser) exploited execute payload delivery. bait documents connect cloud services evade detection second stage delivered phishing page served. see netskope blog . callback persist : after malicious payload executed, malware needs connect c2 (callback) communicate with infected machines, exfiltrate information, establish foothold attackers laterally and\/or dig deeper organization. again, cloud playing important role phase, host infrastructure trusted services. in case compromise services, aws, resources. an attack involve traditional vectors cloud services kill chain activities. netskope calls threats \"hybrid threats\". some phases present. recon persist typically used targeted attacks, malicious actors interested establishing deeper consolidated relationship with victim. " });
