this.add({id:1513, 
title:"Create the AzureEventGridSecureWebhookSubscriber role", 
body:" create azureeventgridsecurewebhooksubscriber role create predefined azure role, azureeventgridsecurewebhooksubscriber allow validation jwt tokens netskope instance. the role makes use azure ad credentials application created step 1 validate jwt tokens. to create azureeventgridsecurewebhooksubscriber role, copy azure_webhook_role.ps1 script locally. # note: before run script ensure logged azure using \"az login\" command.\n\n$webhookappobjectid = \"[replace_with_your_id]\"\n$eventsubscriptionwriterappid \"[replace_with_your_application_id]\" \n\n# start execution\ntry {\n\n creates application role given description\n\n function createapprole([string] $name, [string] $description)\n {\n $approle new-object microsoft.open.azuread.model.approle\n $approle.allowedmembertypes system.collections.generic.list[string]\n $approle.allowedmembertypes.add(\"application\");\n $approle.allowedmembertypes.add(\"user\");\n $approle.displayname $name\n $approle.id new-guid\n $approle.isenabled $true\n $approle.description $description\n $approle.value $name;\n\n return $approle\n }\n\n event grid ad application exists\n\n $eventgridappid \"4962773b-9cdb-44cf-a8bf-237846a00ab7\" you don't need modify id\n $eventgridrolename \"azureeventgridsecurewebhooksubscriber\" name\n $eventgridsp get-azureadserviceprincipal -filter (\"appid eq '\" + \"'\")\n ($eventgridsp -match \"microsoft.eventgrid\")\n write-host \"the defined.`n\"\n } \"creating application\"\n new-azureadserviceprincipal -appid $eventgridappid\n app webhook application\n\n $app get-azureadapplication -objectid $webhookappobjectid\n $approles $app.approles\n\n \"azure app roles addition new role...\"\n $approles\n \n ($approles $eventgridrolename)\n { application: \" $newrole createapprole -name -description role\"\n $approles.add($newrole)\n set-azureadapplication $app.objectid -approles $approles\n\n user assignment create event subscription\n\n $serviceprincipal $app.appid $eventsubscriptionwritersp $eventsubscriptionwriterappid \"'\")\n\n ($null -eq $eventsubscriptionwritersp)\n \"create $eventsubscriptionwriterappid\n try\n assignment: $eventgridapprole $app.approles | where-object -property \"displayname\" -value $eventgridrolename\n new-azureadserviceapproleassignment -id $eventgridapprole.id -resourceid $serviceprincipal.objectid $eventsubscriptionwritersp.objectid -principalid $eventsubscriptionwritersp.objectid\n }\n catch\n if( $_.exception.message -like '*permission assigned exists object*')\n else\n write-error $_.exception.message\n break\n service application\n\n $eventgridsp.objectid $eventgridsp.objectid\n print output references backup\n\n \">> webhook's id: $($app.appid)\"\n objectid $($app.objectid)\"\n}\ncatch exception:\"\n $_\n stacktrace:\" $_.scriptstacktrace\n} log azure portal. you login with ad application administrator role owner service principal webhook app ad. these standard roles defined azure. to learn more: https:\/\/docs.microsoft.com\/en-us\/azure\/active-directory\/roles\/permissions-reference#all-roles on left navigation bar azure portal, click cloud shell button select powershell . using azure powershell, open azure_webhook_role.ps1 update following parameters script. $webhookappobjectid = \" replace_with_object_id_of_application \"\n$eventsubscriptionwriterappid = \"[replace_with_your_application_id]\" refer get the application id and directory id \n$webhookaadtenantid = \" replace_with_your_tenant_id \" enter following commands connect azure ad account with tenant id run script, azure_webhook_role.ps1 . connect-azuread -tenantid $webhookaadtenantid\n.\/azure_webhook_role.ps1 you view azureeventgridsecurewebhooksubscriber role azure app registrations page. the enabled default. " });
