this.add({id:1569, 
title:"Step 2\/2: Configure AWS Permissions for Forensic", 
body:" step 2\/2: configure aws permissions forensic netskope requires permissions perform certain actions aws account creating stack receive cloudwatch events. this screen provides customized cft with required set cross access accounts. the defined updated based services you've enabled accounts & services page. you review cft understand various permissions required netskope. ensure aws account permissions required run netskope iaas services. to complete set must: download cft. in aws account, create new s3 bucket forensic destination. in aws account, upload downloaded cft new cloudformation stack. confirm cross account role with required permissions created. follow detailed instructions complete set up. in permissions screen new setup window, click link download cft. log aws management console using credentials account setting with netskope iaas navigate to  services > storage s3 . create new s3 bucket want netskope store forensic objects. ensure follows naming rules specified aws. to learn bucket naming rules, see aws documentation . navigate services > cloudformation . in cloudformation page, click  create stack . to create stack with new resources, choose with new resources (standard) . to create stack with existing resources, choose with existing resources (import resources) . select  upload template file  and click  choose file  to upload the  aws-instance-setup.yml . click  next . in the specify stack details page, specify a  stack . the stack must: only contain alphanumeric characters hyphens, start with alphabet, exceed128 characters. in parameters section page, specify new s3 bucket created step 3 . click next . in the configure stack options page, use default configuration, click  next . review stack details the  review  page, click acknowledgment click  create stack . when creation process complete, stack displayed cloudformation page. you click stack view details stack. the resources tab displays various components aws-instance-setup.yml . the template tab displays permissions defined template. in netskope ui, confirm cross account role with permissions created aws account. click add accounts . netskope adds aws account settings > api-enabled protection cloud infrastructure page. the page displays services enabled account. once set instance with forensic enabled, create profile. to learn more: creating a forensic profile for public cloud storage . " });
this.add({id:1570, 
title:"What happens in the process?", 
body:" what happens process? netskope lists s3 buckets aws account post instance setup saves metadata database. this enables write download to\/from bucket chosen forensic destination. however, permissions requested single the s3:list -related permissions required netskope aware s3 bucket chosen forensic destination. aws permissions forensics policy purpose s3:getobject this implementation get operation retrieves objects amazon s3. s3:putobject this implementation put operation puts objects violate dlp forensics amazon s3 bucket. s3:listbucket lists specific bucket s3:listallmybuckets this implementation get operation returns list buckets owned authenticated sender request. s3:getbucketlocation this implementation get operation uses location sub-resource return bucket's region. the netskopestack managed netskope manually updated. to learn defining s3 bucket forensic destination: create a forensic profile . " });
