this.add({id:1624, 
title:"Step 1: Creating a Role", 
body:" step 1: creating role netskope requires permissions support log ingestion project successfully. create custom role using cloud shell terminal provided gcp. log console.cloud.google.com . on top-right, click activate cloud shell icon. the cloud shell terminal opens page. on shell prompt, type nano netskope_ueba.yaml press enter\/return key. copy code save file. to save, press ctrl o followed enter\/return key. title: \"netskope_ueba_role\"\ndescription: \"role supporting netskope performing audit log ingestion\"\nstage: \"alpha\"\nincludedpermissions:\n # iam roles check netskope_ueba_role present\n - iam.roles.get\n log sinks created project\n logging.sinks.get\n project metadata list projects organization\n resourcemanager.projects.get execute following command create netskope_ueba_role attach project. replace <project-id> with actual id gcloud iam roles create netskope_ueba_role --project=<project-id> --file=netskope_ueba.yaml to identify project-id , at page, click project selection drop-down list select folder. in search box, type iam click iam & admin . on left navigation, click settings . the ui displays project id . ensure role created executing command below. replace <project-id> with actual id project. gcloud iam roles describe --project=<project-id> netskope_ueba_role " });
