this.add({id:2267, 
title:"Tamperproofing of NS CLient in macOS Ventura", 
body:" tamperproofing ns client macos ventura prior macos ventura versions like monterey older versions, users unaware applications running background. with ventura, displays background allows enable disable them. when netskope client running background disabling services impact functionality end-users encounter security issues. you restrict users enabling option mdms using policies. for example, vmware workspace one, create profiles add custom payloads turn control enable disable allow background section. the following configuration steps restrict users disabling client login items. go resources > profiles&baselines > profiles . click add > add profile . select apple macos platform start. select device profile select context. enter profile name. go custom settings section click add right corner section. the fields enabled now. provide following custom payload information custom settings text-box: <dict>\n <key>payloaddisplayname<\/key>\n <string>service management - managed login items<\/string>\n <key>payloadidentifier<\/key>\n <string>com.apple.servicemanagement.xxx<\/string>\n <key>payloadtype<\/key>\n <string>com.apple.servicemanagement<\/string>\n <key>payloaduuid<\/key>\n <string>xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxx<\/string>\n <key>payloadversion<\/key>\n <integer>1<\/integer><key>rules<\/key>\n <array>\n <key>ruletype<\/key>\n <string>teamidentifier<\/string>\n <key>rulevalue<\/key>\n <string>24w52p9m7w<\/string>\n <\/dict>\n <\/array>\n<\/dict> edit payload identifier uuid values. currently, mdm providers user interface (ui) option disable functionality. hence, use custom settings add payload. click next . on assignment page, assign profile smart groups. click save publish . " });
