this.add({id:2277, 
title:"Additional CLI Commands", 
body:" additional cli commands use ‘help’ command understand different instructions applicable netskope client linux device. for example: to enable netskope client cli quit: ~$ nsclient\nstart process....\n===== netskope client cli,  version: 200.200.0.100 =====\ncopyright(c) 2022 netskope, inc. all rights reserved.\nplease enter <help> available commands.\nnetskope> enable\nenabling client...\nnetskope enable success.\nnetskope> quit to display netskope client status ~$ nsclient\nstart process....\n===== netskope client cli,  version: 99.0.0.1090 =====\ncopyright(c) 2022 netskope, inc. all rights reserved.\nplease enter <help> available commands.\nnetskope> show-status\nnetskope enabled to display netskope client configuration netskope> show-config\nshow configuration progress...     \n netskope client configuration        \n gateway: gateway-qa.de.goskope.com        \n organization: inc        \n gateway ip: 163.116.140.35, pop: us-sfo1        \n user email: jjia@netskope.com        \n configuration: client_config1        \n steering jjia-mygroup2        \n device classification: unmanaged        \n tunnel protocol: tls        \n private access: connected (user tunnel)        \n access 163.116.138.23        \n on-premises check: remote        \n traffic type: all web traffic        \n config updated: 10:27:26,  1st dec, 2022        \n update avaliable.pleasae use <update-config> command latest to display blocked events netskope> show-blocked-event\nblocked event:\napp name: [opera], last access time: thu dec  1 21:01:20 2022 to update client configuration netskope> update-config\nupdate configuration progress...\nstartconfigupdate->bneedupdate=1\nconfiguration update avaliable.\nplease use <update-config> command latest command description --help usage netskope client cli. - enable netskope client status. - disable disable netskope client. - show-status netskope client status. - show-config display netskope client configuration. - update-config update netskope client configuration. - show-blocked-event display netskope client blocked event(s). - set-log-level reset netskope client log level, <debug|info|warning|error|critical> - save-logs save netskope client diagnostic information. - start-pkt start packet capture, <inner|outer> <inner len 0 9999 byte|outer size 99 mb> please use 'stop-pkt' command exit. - stop-pkt stop packet capture. - start-speedtest start speed test, testing <download|upload> <1|10|100>mb file. - show-pa show private access status. " });
