this.add({id:2326, 
title:"Deploy Netskope Client via MST", 
body:" deploy netskope client mst you use mst files deploy netskope client organization units. to clients mst: mst deployment supported netskope client r92 later. create mst deployment file. create deploy gpo with mst targeted devices users. creating mst deployment file the following procedure illustrates steps create mst package using orca database table editor. orca tool available microsoft sdk. you download orca tool learn orca tool, visit orca webpage .   open orca tool goto file > open select netskope client installer (.msi) file. you see list tables installer file. click property view installer property values . select transform > new transform . to deploy netskope client, need add following additional property values table. the fields table combination strings (property value). host - enter tenants add-on url (example: addon-tenantname.example.com ). token - enter tenants organization id. mode - enter peruserconfig (or mode suits deployment needs). autoupdate - enter [ ]. this optional value . if set , client auto updated available version specified configuration. the property entered caps. to add new property value, select property table list right click pane add row . enter property (in caps) click value text box enter value string. repeat add required property values. go transform > generate transform name. this creates mst deployment file. create apply group policy object the following steps illustrate procedure deploy netskope client using created mst package ms group policy objects. open server manager goto tools > group policy management . in group policy management tool, expand domain options locate group policy object option. right click group policy object new . enter deployment. under group policy object option, right click newly created deployment select edit . this opens group policy management editor window. in group policy management editor window, navigate computer configuration > policies > software settings > software installation . right click software installation select new > package select netskope installer (.msi) file. in deploy software pop-up window, select advanced click ok . in netskope client properties window, goto modifications tab. click add select appropriate mst file. link newly created gpo policy target user enforce policy. the following image example. your ou structure vary depending environment . now apply gpo policies. " });
