this.add({id:2329, 
title:"Deploy Client On Windows Using Intune", 
body:" deploy client on windows using intune this article provides instructions deploy netskope client windows devices (either joined active directory azure ad) using microsoft intune. to learn supported os platform, see netskope client supported os and platform section. the following steps deploying netskope client windows devices. prerequisites: on-board add users netskope using directory importer scim integration. ensure device enrolled microsoft intune. log azure portal (portal.azure.com). click more services . click intune . once click intune, redirect endpoint.microsoft.com. from microsoft endpoint manager admin center, select apps . select add . for app type, select “line-of-business app”. upload nsclient.msi app package file select ok . under app information: provide description. publisher name. set ignore app version yes intend allow netskope client auto-update. select appropriate category. select no display featured app company portal . information privacy url optional values. under command-line arguments: token= <organization id> host=addon- <tenant-name> .goskope.com mode=peruserconfig (use peruserconfig multi-user environments) autoupdate=on (only applicable want client auto-update) \/qn select ok . select appropriate scope tag. select add . wait app upload finalize select netskope client app list. select assignments > add group . for assignment type, select required . select appropriate groups included excluded. select save . you monitor installation process intune. go client apps > install status > search “ netskope ” > device install status . " });
this.add({id:2330, 
title:"Uninstalling Clients", 
body:" uninstalling clients to set un-installion script netskope client windows devices follow procedure described section: this procedure applicable devices ad joined. also, subsequent installation, un-assign app avoid un-installation newly installed clients. login intune admin console select device configuration . in device configuration page, click scripts option left hand side. to start adding uninstallation script, click add button select windows 10 . in add powershell script page, enter name script configuration click next continue. in script settings page, select powershell computer. enter following command script. $product_identifier= get-wmiobject -class win32_product | name -eq \"netskope client\" select -expandproperty identifyingnumber\nmsiexec \/uninstall $product_identifier \/qn \/l*v <path-to>\\nscuninstall.log set following options script: run script using logged credentials - yes enforce script signature check - no run script 64 bit powershell host - yes modify path log written failure modify, results script failure. the logged user permission run write specified directory change run script using logged credentials no run context. if running context, user permission write specified directory. click next continue. in assignment step, assign user groups script. netskope client devices assigned group uninstalled. in step, review selections click add complete procedure. " });
this.add({id:2331, 
title:"Deploy Client on macOS Using Intune", 
body:" deploy client macos using intune this article provides instructions deploy netskope client macos devices(big sur later) using microsoft intune. the following steps deploying devices running 11.x (big sur) later. prerequisites devices running macos 11.x (big sur) later. enroll devices microsoft's endpoint manager download netskope root intermediate certificates convert .cer extension. to learn more, see certificates configure verify saml forward proxy authentication ensure users properly imported netskope tenant. to learn user provisioning forward proxy authentication, see provisioning and authentication deployment procedure perform following steps deploy client macos using intune: sign microsoft intune admin center. go devices > macos devices . ensure devices install netskope client listed. create configuration profiles deploy netskope certificates. go macos policies > configuration profiles > create profile select profile type templates template trusted certificate . click create . the page refresh with settings. enter root certificate profile click next . click folder icon select netskope root certificate (.cer file) click next continue. assign appropriate device group click next . review configuration click create . repeat steps used upload netskope root certificate create configuration profile intermediate certificate. validate certificate chain you validate complete certificate chain mac keychain. download netskope intune configuration script netskope support portal . extract contents mac-mdm-script.zip file. open script text editor search commented line update intune deployment . update script options parameters 4 8 follows mode: deployment modes configuration parameters standard mode (email-based) parameter 4: your tenant name. if url https:\/\/addon-corp.goskope.com, enter addon-corp. parameter 5: your ad name. parameter 6: for rel 89 before: enter rest api token. for rel 90.2 later: your organization id. for example, set -- 0 <addon-host> <ad> <org id\/ rest api token> upn mode parameter 4: your addon url. if tenant url https:\/\/corp.goskope.com, addon-corp.goskope.com. parameter 5: your organization id. parameter 6: enter keyword upn (lowercase). for example, set -- 0 <addon-host> <org id> upn multi-user mode (enabling provisioned user tenant) parameter 4: your addon url. if tenant url https:\/\/corp.goskope.com, enter addon-corp.goskope.com. parameter 5: your organization id. parameter 6: enter keyword peruserconfig. for example, set -- 0 <username> <addon-host> <ad> <org id> peruserconfig idp single-user mode parameter 4: enter idp specify client deployment mode idp. parameter 5: domain name. example, tenant url https:\/\/corp.goskope.com, enter goskope.com. parameter 6: tenant name. example: if tenant url https:\/\/corp.goskope.com, enter corp. parameter 7: email address request option. enter 0, want user's email address. 1 for example, set -- 0 1 idp <tenant domain name> 0\/1 idp multi-user mode parameter 4: enter idp specify client deployment mode. parameter 5: domain name. example, tenant url https:\/\/corp.goskope.com, enter goskope.com. parameter 6: tenant name. example: if tenant url https:\/\/corp.goskope.com, enter corp. parameter 7: email address request option. enter 0, want user email address. 1 user's parameter 8: enter peruserconfig specify multi-user idp deployment mode. for example, set -- 0 1 idp <tenant domain name> < tenant 0\/1 peruserconfig for macos devices (single-user installations) ad joined parameter 4 : your tenant url. for rel 89 before: if tenant url corp.goskope.com, enter corp.goskope.com. for rel 90.2 later: if tenant url https:\/\/corp.goskope.com, enter addon-corp.goskope.com. parameter 5: for rel 89 before: enter rest api token. for rel 90.2 later: your organization id. parameter 6: preferences file (plist)  name. when entering filename, enter complete filename including .plist extension. example: netskope.plist . do add http url file. parameter 7 : enter keyword preference_email. for example, set -- 0 <addon-host> <org id> <plist file name> <preference_email> save script. go devices > macos > shell scripts click add . enter name click next . select script ( .sh file ) local storage computer. make following changes: run script signed users - no hide script notifications devices - yes script frequency - every 30 minutes max number times retry script fails - 3 times . assign script groups, users, and\/or devices. click next continue. click add add script push devices. go macos policies > configuration profiles > create profile select profile type templates . under template names select extensions click create . provide netskope system extension profile click next . expand system extensions configure allow systems extensions follows: bundle identifier : com.netskope.client.netskope-client.netskopeclientmacappproxy team identifier : 24w52p9m7w select next continue. assign appropriate users device group select next . review configuration click create . use profiles options end-user device validate system extension was deployed successfully. go macos policies > configuration profiles download custom configuration profiles netskope support portal . select create profile profile types option, select templates > custom . click create . specify profile name. keep deployment channel option device channel . upload custom configuration profile downloaded netskope support portal. click next continue. select assign appropriate users groups. click next continue. review configuration click create . use profiles option end-user device validate installation was successful. create line-of-business applications deployed apple devices (big sur). go apps > macos click add . select line-of-business app app type drop-down menu click select . click select app file browse upload app package. click ok . enter publisher click next . assign application devices users. click next continue. click create complete creating application. now login idp start enrollment process. idp enrollment workflow the following steps illustrate client enrollment workflow microsoft intune. after complete steps deploy netskope client intune, receive notification allow proxy configurations. click allow . in enroll netskope client, enter email address. click next . enter tenant select domain shared with user respective it. now, sign using authentication credential complete enrollment process. " });
