this.add({id:3018, 
title:"Microsoft Defender for Endpoint Plugin for Threat Exchange", 
body:" microsoft defender endpoint plugin threat exchange this document explains how configure microsoft defender atp integration with threat exchange module netskope cloud platform. allows sharing file hashes netskope. fetched indicator types: url, md5, sha256 shared indicator types: url, md5, sha256 high-level use cases: indicators types ip, domains, url microsoft defender endpoint fetched urls netskope cloud exchange. indicators type url differentiated ip, url, domain, ingested microsoft defender endpoint. action mappings plugin version v1.1.0 v1.2.0 actions plugin v1.1.0 action plugin v1.2.0 unknown audit allow allowed block block alert alert warn alertandblock blockandremediate for actions audit, alert, alertandblock, select generate alert checkbox microsoft defender endpoint alerts generated. prerequisites to complete configuration, need: a netskope tenant (or multiple, example, production development\/test instances). a secure web gateway subscription url sharing. a netskope cloud exchange with threat exchange module configured. a microsoft defender endpoint account. your microsoft azure tenant id, client secret. a microsoft azure application with ti.readwrite.all permission. for information, article . connectivity hosts required https:\/\/api.securitycenter.microsoft.com\/api\/indicators https:\/\/securitycenter.windows.com https:\/\/login.microsoftonline.com https:\/\/portal.azure.com workflow create custom file profile. get directory tenant id, application client secret. configure microsoft defenderfor endpoint plugin. configure sharing netskope microsoft defender endpoint. validate microsoft defenderfor endpoint plugin. " });
this.add({id:3019, 
title:"Create a Secure Web Gateway Custom File Profile", 
body:" create secure web gateway custom file profile in netskope ui, policies , select file , click new file profile . click file hash left panel, select sha256 file hash dropdown list. enter temporary value text field. netskope does support progressing having field, recommends entering string 64 characters consists character f . for example, ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff . this low possibility matching valid file format. click next . enter profile name description. we recommend having blank spaces profile name; use underscores spaces. click save . to publish profile tenant, click apply changes right. " });
this.add({id:3020, 
title:"Create an Application and get your Tenant ID, Application ID, and Client Secret", 
body:" create application tenant id, client secret log azure with account global administrator role. go azure active directory > app registrations . in registration form, enter application, click register . copy directory (tenant) id application (client) application page. click add certificate secret click new client secret generate client secret. add description expire time, the. click add . copy secret value; displayed once. to enable app access defender endpoint, application page, select api permissions > add permission apis organization uses , enter windowsdefenderatp , select windowsdefenderatp . on application permission tab, select ti permissions list, enable ti.readwrite.all checkbox basis requirement, click add permissions . select grant admin consent application, click yes confirmation. " });
this.add({id:3021, 
title:"Configure the Microsoft Defender for Endpoint Plugin", 
body:" configure microsoft defender endpoint plugin in threat exchange, settings click plugins . select microsoft defender endpoint plugin box open plugin creation pages. enter select basic information first page: configuration name: enter appropriate integration. poll interval: adjust environment needs. we recommend 5 minutes production environments. aging criteria: leave default. override reputation: leave default. enable ssl verification: leave default. click next . enter select configuration parameters second page: tenant id: enter directory (tenant) id. app id: enter application (client) id. app secret: enter client secret values. region: select appropriate region. ioc source: enter use description field sharing iocs defender. initial range (in days): leave default. click save . go threat exchange > plugins see new defender endpoint plugin. " });
