this.add({id:3086, 
title:"Development Guidelines", 
body:" development guidelines use package directory structure python code. make sure 3rd-party libraries packaged with plugin package checked known vulnerabilities. make sure follow standard python code conventions. run verify flake8 lint check passes with docstring enabled. for scripts\/integrations written python, make sure create unit tests documented here. plugin architecture allows storing states; however, avoid huge objects state management. check python code any vulnerabilities. the plugin icon 10kb. make sure use company logo(and product’s) with transparent background . recommended size logo 300 x 50 similar aspect ratio. use checkpoint provided threat exchange core than implementing own. follow plugin directory structure . make sure map various fields received api calls with indicator data model leverage benefit system. fields like reputation, first-seen, comments so indicator makes sense soc user analyzing data. comment field gives context analyst. the include file (in case hash). convert time-stamp values human-readable format (from epoch datetime object). use proper validation parameters passed validate method provide help text parameters. use notifier object raise notification failures critical situations (like rate-limiting, exceeding payload size) notify status plugin user. make sure implement proper logging mechanism with logger object passed threat exchange platform. helps ops team troubleshooting. any sensitive data logged leaked notification. have meaningful proper type plugin configuration parameters. proxy dict ssl certificate validation flag passed threat exchange platform. " });
