this.add({id:3212, 
title:"Configure the Microsoft O365 Exchange server and the upstream MTA in the Netskope tenant", 
body:" configure microsoft o365 exchange server upstream mta netskope tenant in netskope ui, settings > security cloud platform > smtp . under microsoft office 365 exchange , click edit . in edit microsoft office 365 exchange settings window: email server setting : copy enter fqdn microsoft office 365 exchange route emails netskope cloud. you require configuring smtp proxy connector admin center. email domain next hop : enter following information. netskope use information associate emails with real-time protection policies . domain : enter verify primary domain want use email processing. you enter domain, subdomain, wildcard (e.g., abc.com, cde.abc.com, *.abc.com). to learn finding microsoft o365: finding the microsoft o365 exchange tenant id and primary domain . configure mail from domains. if not, emails domain rejected. tenant id : enter tenant id, directory id box properties page. to learn finding tenant id microsoft o365: finding the microsoft o365 exchange tenant id and primary domain . next hop : enter ip address\/fqdn port upstream mta want emails routed. click +add add multiple domain entries. select set tenant id next hop each domain want enter unique tenant id hope domain entry. click save . " });
