this.add({id:3406, 
title:"SCIM-Based User Provisioning", 
body:" scim-based user provisioning system cross-domain identity management (scim) defines standard exchanging identity information different cloud app vendors. the objects exchanged using scim called resources (like user resource, group resource etc). the purpose automate exchange apps provisioning.  a scim-enabled directory server (like azure ad okta) directly send user information scim netskope cloud. this service currently available microsoft okta oauth token authentication. to begin integrating with scim authentication services, need create unique oauth token. you token directory tools page. access page: go settings > tools directory . in directory tools page, scim integration tab click add token . enter client name click save . now, log scim application account set app post new user details server. to set application, need scim server url (also known application endpoint url) scim integration tab directory tools page. for specific integration instructions, to: azure scim integration okta scim integration follow instructions specified respective applications app provision users. once complete, test connection. if succeeds, scim integration process complete. for details integrations with azure okta, to: microsoft azure: https:\/\/docs.microsoft.com\/en-us\/azure\/active-directory\/active-directory-scim-provisioning okta: https:\/\/developer.okta.com\/standards\/scim\/ microsoft azure support netskope currently supports following: provisioning users. provisioning groups. okta support netskope currently supports following: provisioning users user groups. " });
