this.add({id:3470, 
title:"Device Classification with Tanium for Windows", 
body:" device classification with tanium windows the netskope tanium integration enables joint customers leverage tanium’s high-fidelity endpoint data user-friendly natural language search capabilities determine endpoint’s overall posture equates compliant , safe , managed . these endpoint posture dispositions, determined one-time recurring basis, drive decision netskope treat differently than non-compliant, risky, unmanaged device. utilizing adaptive policy controls, user non-compliant device able download upload files risky posture, perform basic functions, browsing web, sending email, etc. once tanium finds device compliant again, flag endpoint enabling netskope determine new state, match policy, example, let user files around, knowing making decisions, potentially compromised host.   of course, users can’t benefit netskope’s protection capabilities isn’t deployed up-to-date. leveraging tanium’s software management configuration capabilities, ensure latest netskope steering client deployed, installed, active managed hosts. here's illustration how netskope tanium work together. click play watch video netskope tanium integration. " });
this.add({id:3471, 
title:"Integrate Tanium with Netskope for Windows", 
body:" integrate tanium with netskope windows create following saved questions: saved question name tanium question netskope installed windows get computer name machines with installed applications contains netskope client netskope not installed windows get computer name machines with ( is windows contains true installed applications netskope client ) netskope managed windows get computer name machines with registry value data[hkey_local_machine\\software\\netskope\\provisioning,managed] contains 1 netskope unmanaged windows get computer name machines with registry value data[hkey_local_machine\\software\\netskope\\provisioning,managed] contains 0 netskope running windows get computer name machines with running service contains netskope client netskope stopped windows get computer name machines with stopped service contains netskope client these saved questions organized dashboard category browsing interact home. create following packages: package name package command netskope health - managed cmd \/c ..\\..\\tpython\\tpython netskope_tanium_3_0_0.py -ns -s enable netskope health - unmanaged cmd \/c ..\\..\\tpython\\tpython netskope_tanium_3_0_0.py -ns -s disable -v 0 netskope installer windows cmd \/c msiexec \/i nsclient_addon-<your tenant>.goskope.com_###_.msi please contact netskope tanium account manager client installation python script package files. create scheduled actions managed unmanaged policies: using interact targeting question results managed, compliant, safe, select deploy action pick package netskope health – managed . using interact targeting question results unmanaged, non-compliant, risky, select deploy action pick package netskope health – unmanaged . see following example targeting question based tanium patch compliance: https:\/\/community.tanium.com\/s\/article\/use-tanium-patch-data-to-determine-if-systems-are-out-of-compliance-with-slas optional: using interact, run targeting question netskope agent installation. select deploy action pick netskope installer package created step #2 this data visualized tanium trends. please contact technical account manager (tam) details. in netskope tenant settings > manage device classification , click new device classification rule , select windows . enter parameters: enter rule name. under classification criteria, select registry . select hkey_local_machine , enter \\software\\netskope\\provisioning key, enter managed value. select reg_sz enter 1 data. click save . a match registry value constitutes managed . " });
