this.add({id:3574, 
title:"Customize Table Columns", 
body:" customize table columns use customize columns dialog box specify information want see application events page table. general : includes activity, traffic type, access method, managed application, browser information. user : includes username, ip address, host name, os, preferred data location (pdl), device type, classification, user group, ou information. application : includes application, category , object, site, ccl, cci, instance id, url, object type, tags, app suite, name, sanctioned (appears selected policy creation data found, column appears field blank). alert : includes type, policy name, dlp profile rule action, incident id information. source : includes source ip address, location, region, zip code, country information. destination : includes destination ip address, location, region, country information. click restore defaults restore column-related default settings. " });
this.add({id:3575, 
title:"About Endpoint Events", 
body:" about endpoint events with endpoint data loss protection (dlp) , netskope monitors users usb storage devices policy violations. you view user device activities haven't violated skope it > endpoint events . when events violate device content control policies, netskope generates alert event, view skope it alerts ( skope it  >  alerts ). events violate content control policies trigger dlp incident ( incidents > dlp ). " });
this.add({id:3576, 
title:"Viewing Device Events", 
body:" viewing device events to view events triggered device control policies organization, to  skope it  >  endpoint events > device . on device events page, can: refresh device results. filter device events specific time frame. you use predefined frame choose  date range  to use calendar time menus customize own. search filter device events user. click  + add filter add filters narrow search results. you click save filter combination future searches. view list device events. for event, see following information: time (default) activity (default) usb device name (default) user (default) computer name (default) event type\n offline event usb device id\n usb device sn usb device type model manufacturer os user name os\n os details policy name\n policy name enforced policy version policy action policy action enforced click view information device event. following helpful fields investigating event: manufacturer : the manufacturer usb device, stored device. this text usb-if-issued vendor id. device id : the instance id device. device sn : the serial number device. device type : the device class. model : the model usb device. this text numeric product id. device : the device. sort table time device events occurred. export device events (up 500,000 rows) csv file. click customize table columns restore default ones. view 100 device events page. view multiple pages table. " });
this.add({id:3577, 
title:"Viewing Content Events", 
body:" viewing content events to view events triggered content control policies organization, to  skope it  >  endpoint events > content . on content events page, can: refresh content results. filter content events specific time frame. you use predefined frame choose  date range  to use calendar time menus customize own. search filter content events user. click  + add filter add filters narrow search results. you click save filter combination future searches. view list content events. for event, see following information: time (default) file name (default) activity (default) usb device name (default) user (default) computer name (default) file directory\n file path executable hash executable signed file md5 file sha256 file origin file size file type event type\n offline event usb device id\n usb device sn usb device type model manufacturer os user name dlp profile name\n dlp rule os\n os details pid process cert subject process name process path policy name policy name enforced policy version policy action policy action enforced click view information content event. following helpful fields investigating event: file type : the type file. size (bytes) : the file size bytes. file directory : the directory file stored. file name : the file. file path : the file path. process id : the process id performs file operation. process name : the process performs file operation. process path : the path executable process performs file operation. md5 : the md5 hash file. you use value filter skope it events view activity associated with sha256 : the sha-256 hash file. you use value filter skope it events view activity associated with sort table time content events occurred. export content events (up 500,000 rows) csv file. click customize table columns restore default ones. view 100 content events page. view multiple pages table. " });
